---
// The positive flip right after Stakes — repurposed from the fields
// that used to back the old collapsible "Explanatory paragraph" trigger
// (storybrand_pitch/storybrand_pitch_label), now the visible heading +
// body of a standalone section, on Homepage rows only. The Explanatory
// Paragraph's own full-brandscript fields (see ExplanatoryBrandscript.
// astro) replaced the old collapsible role. Renders nothing when
// storybrand_pitch is empty — same never-show-an-empty-shell discipline
// as every other optional StoryBrand section.
//
// No image — a real client working session preferred this over the
// original image-beside-text layout once populated with real content
// (a 3-item short list read better as 3 cards than as prose next to a
// photo). Card mode (benefits.length > 0) stays centered — a centered
// heading over a centered card grid, matching PlanSteps.astro's own
// convention — and gets the wider max-w-5xl a 3-column grid needs. The
// plain-prose fallback below is a different shape (a markdown block,
// possibly including a bullet list) and follows Section.astro's own
// "prose section" convention instead: max-w-3xl, left-aligned, no
// centering — centering a <ul> centers each line's text while its
// bullet marker stays pinned to the list's own left inset, which is
// exactly the "bullet far from its own text" bug a real client caught
// live on Luke Burgett's page (2026-09-18). See Section.astro's own
// comment for the fuller writeup of this convention. Reuses
// lib/markdown.ts's
// extractShortBenefitList() to turn 3 consecutive `### heading` +
// paragraph pairs into real card data, the same pattern
// StoryBrandSection.astro already uses for storybrand_success — not a
// new detection mechanism. Falls back to plain centered prose
// (beforeHtml/afterHtml) for any content that isn't shaped that way,
// so this is a safe drop-in regardless of what a given client's copy
// looks like. The 3-card grid is a local `sm:grid-cols-3` here, not
// FeatureGrid.astro (which is hard-coded to 2 columns) — adding a
// 3-column variant to that shared component for this one call site
// wasn't worth the added complexity there.
import { extractShortBenefitList } from '../lib/markdown';

interface Props {
  heading?: string | null;
  body: string | null;
  ctaText?: string | null;
}

const { heading, body, ctaText } = Astro.props;
const { beforeHtml, benefits, afterHtml } = extractShortBenefitList(body);
---

{body && (
  <section class="py-14">
    <div class:list={['mx-auto px-6', benefits.length > 0 ? 'max-w-5xl text-center' : 'max-w-3xl']}>
      {heading && (
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-center font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-brand-ink">
          {heading}
        </h2>
      )}
      {beforeHtml && <div class:list={['prose', benefits.length > 0 && 'mx-auto']} set:html={beforeHtml} />}

      {benefits.length > 0 && (
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
          {benefits.map((benefit) => (
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white p-6 text-center shadow-md transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl">
              <h3 class="mb-2 font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] font-bold text-brand-ink">{benefit.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">{benefit.description}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      )}

      {afterHtml && <div class:list={['prose mt-6', benefits.length > 0 && 'mx-auto']} set:html={afterHtml} />}

      {ctaText && (
        <div class="mt-8 text-center">
          <a
            href="#lead-generator"
            class="inline-block rounded-md bg-brand-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:opacity-90 hover:shadow-md"
          >
            {ctaText}
          </a>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
)}
